{"id":"CVE-2008-1948","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2008-05-21T10:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T08:41:00.219Z","description":"The _gnutls_server_name_recv_params function in lib/ext_server_name.c in libgnutls in gnutls-serv in GnuTLS before 2.2.4 does not properly calculate the number of Server Names in a TLS 1.0 Client Hello message during extension handling, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (crash) or possibly execute arbitrary code via a zero value for the length of Server Names, which leads to a buffer overflow in session resumption data in the pack_security_parameters function, aka GNUTLS-SA-2008-1-1.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/30331","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"30331"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/31939","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"31939"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/usn-613-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-613-1"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-security-announce/2008-09/msg00003.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"SUSE-SA:2008:046"},{"url":"http://www.redhat.com/support/errata/RHSA-2008-0492.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2008:0492"},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2008/05/20/1","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20080520 Re: CVE ID request: GNUTLS"},{"url":"http://security.gentoo.org/glsa/glsa-200805-20.xml","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-200805-20"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/30355","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"30355"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/30317","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"30317"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/