{"id":"CVE-2008-2377","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2008-08-08T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T08:58:02.218Z","description":"Use-after-free vulnerability in the _gnutls_handshake_hash_buffers_clear function in lib/gnutls_handshake.c in libgnutls in GnuTLS 2.3.5 through 2.4.0 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (crash) or possibly execute arbitrary code via TLS transmission of data that is improperly used when the peer calls gnutls_handshake within a normal session, leading to attempted access to a deallocated libgcrypt handle.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://article.gmane.org/gmane.comp.encryption.gpg.gnutls.devel/2947","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[gnutls-devel] 20080630 GnuTLS 2.4.1"},{"url":"https://issues.rpath.com/browse/RPL-2650","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.gnu.org/software/gnutls/security.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.nabble.com/Details-on-the-gnutls_handshake-local-crash-problem--GNUTLS-SA-2008-2--td18205022.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[gnutls-devel] 20080630 Details on the gnutls_handshake local crash problem [GNUTLS-SA-2008-2]"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2008/2398","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2008-2398"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/30713","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"30713"},{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/44486","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"gnutls-gnutlshandshake-code-execution(44486)"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/31505","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"31505"}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2008-4989","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2008-11-13T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T10:31:28.318Z","description":"The _gnutls_x509_verify_certificate function in lib/x509/verify.c in libgnutls in GnuTLS before 2.6.1 trusts certificate chains in which the last certificate is an arbitrary trusted, self-signed certificate, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to insert a spoofed certificate for any Distinguished Name (DN).","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDVSA-2008:227","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDVSA-2008:227"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/usn-678-2","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-678-2"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/33694","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"33694"},{"url":"http://security.gentoo.org/glsa/glsa-200901-10.xml","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-200901-10"},{"url":"http://www.redhat.com/support/errata/RHSA-2008-0982.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2008:0982"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/678-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-678-1"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/498431/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20081117 rPSA-2008-0322-1 gnutls"},{"url":"http://article.gmane.org/gmane.comp.encryption.gpg.gnutls.devel/3215","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[gnutls-devel] 20081110 GnuTLS 2.6.1 - Security release [GNUTLS-SA-2008-3]"},{"url":"http://article.gmane.org/gmane.comp.encryption.gpg.gnutls.devel/3217","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[gnutls-devel] 20081110 Analysis of vulnerability GNUTLS-SA-2008-3 CVE-2008-4989"},{"url":"http://wiki.rpath.com/Advisories:rPSA-2008-0322","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIR